# Oracle 10.2.0.5's reply to JDBC thin 11.2's CREATE_TEMP of a CLOB (#2803): the
# new locator, the charset (873), the SCN slot (`81 02`, negative), the amount 1, the status.
# Captured 2026-11-27 through tools/capture_proxy.py. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  08 00 26 00 01 02 08 80  03 00 02 00 00 fb 36 91  |..&...........6.|
00000010  00 00 00 00 01 03 69 00  0a 00 00 00 01 00 00 00  |......i.........|
00000020  00 15 b1 c3 03 ac f1 78  24 02 03 69 81 02 01 01  |.......x$..i....|
00000030  04 01 01 01 06 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000040  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  03 00 01 01 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000050
